# Mobile-first responsive layouts

The authenticated Produza panel must work from narrow phones (~375px) through tablets to desktop. Layout work is **mobile-first**: base styles target the smallest viewport; enhance with MUI breakpoints (`sm` / `md` / `lg`). Do not invent a separate mobile visual language — keep design-system parity (`design-system.mdc`).

Related: `design-system.mdc` (shell/theme), `ux-feedback.mdc` (toasts/loadings), `produza-react-typescript.mdc` (MUI `sx` / styled).

## Breakpoints (MUI)

- Prefer `theme.breakpoints.up('sm'|'md'|'lg')` in `styled(...)` and `sx={{ … }}`.
- Default styles = **xs**. Add rules only as the viewport grows.
- Prefer `sx={{ px: { xs: 2, sm: 3, md: 4 } }}` over desktop-only fixed padding/width.
- Use `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.up('md'))` for structural behavior switches (e.g. permanent vs temporary nav), not for painting brand colors.

## Shell and navigation

- Below `md`, the sidebar is a **temporary** drawer opened from the header; do not keep a permanent rail that shrinks content on phones.
- At `md+`, keep the permanent drawer (expand/collapse) as today.
- Page gutters live on shared page chrome (`PageRoot` / shell breadcrumbs) with responsive `px` — avoid stacking large fixed horizontal paddings that collapse usable width.
- Breadcrumbs, headers, and hero/action rows must wrap; titles may use responsive type size and `overflowWrap`.

## Tables, filters, forms, wizards

| Surface | Mobile-first rule |
|--------|-------------------|
| List filters | No desktop-only `minWidth` that exceeds the content column; fields stretch full width on `xs`, tighten from `sm` |
| Data tables | Always allow horizontal scroll (`overflowX: 'auto'`) or stack into cards; never force multi-column tables to overflow the viewport without a scroll container |
| Table footers / pagers | `flexWrap`; stack summary + pager on `xs` |
| Form / editor / detail bodies | Responsive padding (`xs` tighter → `md` roomier) |
| Form / modal / wizard actions | Stack full-width on `xs` (`column-reverse` so primary is first); row + wrap from `sm` |
| Create wizards / steppers | Compact or vertical on small screens; horizontal + `alternativeLabel` from `sm`+ |
| Recipe / floor step rows | Single column on `xs`; multi-column grids only from `md` |
| Drawers / dialogs | Paper `width: 100%` with viewport margins; actions wrap on narrow screens |

## Prefer shared fixes

When breakage is structural (shell, page padding, table scroll, form actions), fix **`AppShell` / `AppSidebar` / `AppHeader` / shared `page` / shared dialog** — or the shared pattern mirrored across raw-materials / products / production-orders — instead of one-off page hacks.

## Do not

- Hardcode desktop-only widths (`minWidth: 240`, fixed `720`, etc.) that break ~375px content columns.
- Leave permanent sidebar consuming space on phones.
- Ship wide tables or need-lines without an overflow/scroll wrapper.
- Redesign visuals for “mobile look” beyond responsive spacing, wrapping, and navigation behavior.
